<title>FRANCE: EU cuts refund on durum semolina exports - ONIC.</title>
<headline>EU cuts refund on durum semolina exports - ONIC.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday cut the daily refund on exports of durum wheat semolina to 10 Ecus per tonne from Wednesday's level of 15 Ecus, France's grain office ONIC said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday the EU had already lowered the refund to 15 Ecus from 24.50 previously, it said.</p>
<p>The lower semolina rebate followed news that the EU granted exports of 3,400 tonnes of free-market durum wheat at a rebate of 6.48 Ecus per tonne in a trial tender to export 100,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
